WEBVTT

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:17.430
Here we go!
The time has finally come.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.560
The final match of the first stage
will begin shortly.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.020
<i>Fang! Fang!</i>

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.150
GAOLAN WONGSAWAT

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.320
What's going on?

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.830
<i>The whole stadium is shaking.</i>

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.080
All the spectators are waiting
for Fang to appear...

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.000
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI - JUN SEKIBAYASHI

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.120
...and believe he's the one to win.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.210
That's a poor situation for his opponent

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.380
but maybe not for Ohkubo, I guess.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.720
It's such a favorable situation
for a pro-wrestler, though.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.720
<i>Fang.</i>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.440
<i>Bring it on, the fifth Fang.</i>

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.900
<i>"Bring it on," you said?</i>

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.570
<i>It seems you don't understand.</i>

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.530
<i>What...?</i>

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.360
<i>This is just a game for me.</i>

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.030
<i>Prove it to us.</i>

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.040
<i>That you even have fangs.</i>

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:30.460
<i>I kept you waiting for a long time.</i>
<i>Now I have a fang that can kill you.</i>

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.340
Are you going to take your revenge
in this tournament, Wakatsuki?

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.880
Nah, I don't think that's going to happen.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.600
Because I'm going to be the one
who takes Fang's head.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.980
Let me warn you.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.810
Don't think of Fang as a human.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:52.020
He's a powerful, violent disaster.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.400
So, you're saying he's like a monster?

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.700
NAOYA OHKUBO

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.280
That sounds super fun.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.370
Okay. Time to bust that monster.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:08.420
<i>The King of Combat, Naoya Ohkubo,</i>
<i>enters the field.</i>

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:43.930
CHAMPIONS

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.600
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.600
KENGAN MATCH

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.940
<i>Let's welcome the fighters!</i>

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.650
GAME 16

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:00.190
<i>The self-proclaimed</i>
<i>Rocky of Osaka is here.</i>

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.650
SAYAKA KATAHARA

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.950
Currently at the center of the MMA world

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.490
is this Japanese fighter known as
the King of Combat.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.830
<i>His blows are unparalleled.</i>

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.330
<i>His throws are lethal.</i>

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.300
<i>His locks are inescapable.</i>

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:23.630
<i>And his holds make you faint in a second.</i>

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.720
<i>He's flawless in every way!</i>

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:32.180
<i>His MMA record is 26 wins and no losses.</i>

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:38.690
<i>The living legend of MMA</i>
<i>is now entering the kengan world!</i>

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.690
<i>Standing at 195 cm and weighing 116 kg,</i>

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.610
<i>he makes his kengan match debut today.</i>

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.280
Representing Muji Television Network,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:54.410
<i>also known as the King of Combat,</i>
<i>Naoya Ohkubo!</i>

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.460
Hello, everyone.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.180
Your Naoya Ohkubo is here.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.850
GENSAI KUROKI

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:10.930
RINO KURAYOSHI - REI MIKAZUCHI

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.020
SEISHU AKOYA

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.350
<i>This man must be... strong.</i>

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:22.030
<i>Another man's flesh for me to taste.</i>

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.650
RAIAN KURE

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:27.530
<i>There's nothing like beating</i>
<i>the shit out of a strong guy.</i>

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.200
<i>I'm so thrilled.</i>

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:34.250
<i>Don't get killed by the Fang</i>
<i>before I get to fight you.</i>

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.620
<i>My next opponent is a wimp</i>

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.250
<i>who had a hard time</i>
<i>dealing with the Inaba Style.</i>

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.960
OHMA TOKITA - KAZUO YAMASHITA

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.550
Whoa, that's cool!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.470
He looks totally different
from who he usually is.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.390
<i>I knew it all along, Naoya Ohkubo.</i>

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.640
<i>Of all those four,</i>

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.560
<i>you are the strongest.</i>

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.280
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for your patience.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.950
<i>It is finally time for that man</i>
<i>to make his entrance.</i>

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.830
What's going on?
It got quiet all of a sudden.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.880
<i>Since his debut match,</i>
<i>he's been on a record-breaking streak</i>

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.210
of 157 consecutive wins on kengan matches.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:29.180
He's the man who built a new legend
and a mountain of corpses.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.970
<i>Now, he is entering the battlefield.</i>

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:37.770
<i>Standing at 201 cm and weighing 128 kg,</i>

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:43.110
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>157 wins and no losses.</i>

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:50.320
His total acquired assets are seven
trillion, 706 billion, 83 million yen.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:56.750
Representing Dainippon Bank,
also known as Fang of Metsudo,

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.630
Agito Kanoh!

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.720
AGITO KANOH
REPRESENTATIVE FIGHTER OF DAINIPPON BANK

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.390
<i>Finally...</i>

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.470
<i>it's time...</i>

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:22.020
to start the main event!

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.110
This is it!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.490
This is the match I've been waiting for.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:33.820
METSUDO KATAHARA

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.830
Aren't we excited for this, Atami?

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:37.870
HISASHI ATAMI
CHAIRMAN MUJI TELEVISION NETWORK

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.000
Very much.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.120
I can hardly wait!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.920
Fang! Fang!

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.510
What the hell?
This is one hell of a cheer.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.510
Can't any of you root for me?

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.890
But, man...

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.550
Jeez. You are something.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:59.680
Just by looking at you,
I can tell you're incredibly strong.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.770
You're not even human anymore.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.770
In RPG games, you'd be the strongest enemy
that awaits me at the very final stage.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.940
But you know what?

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:14.320
The last boss is always defeated
by a human hero in the end,

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:19.200
and I am the strongest human!

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:22.750
Let's get started
with the last boss busting.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.210
"Last Boss"?

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.750
I've never heard of that fighter.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.510
Oh, man. Now is not the time
for making jokes.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:35.930
This "Last Boss" you speak of...
what fighting style does he use?

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:38.760
Are you being serious?
It's so hard to communicate with you!

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.350
<i>Jeez, he's far too detached</i>
<i>from the real world.</i>

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.390
<i>But anyway...</i>

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:49.690
<i>this ridiculous pressure he's giving off</i>
<i>is definitely in the last boss class.</i>

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.650
<i>Cool.</i>

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:57.530
<i>Ohkubo takes an orthodox MMA-style stance.</i>

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:03.910
<i>On the other hand, Agito takes</i>
<i>an offensive stance with a lowered guard.</i>

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:08.170
<i>Both fighters are ready for battle.</i>

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:14.550
<i>Which one is stronger?</i>

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.850
<i>I long to witness the result</i>
<i>as soon as possible!</i>

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:21.560
Fight!

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:27.690
Wha...

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.960
<i>Thirty-four seconds into the match,</i>

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.760
<i>Naoya Ohkubo succeeds in a takedown.</i>

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.480
A NEW STAR APPEARS IN
MIDDLE SCHOOL WRESTLING

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.440
<i>Naoya Ohkubo's fighting career</i>
<i>started in a wrestling club</i>

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.650
<i>in his first year of middle school.</i>

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.530
NAOYA OHKUBO WINS CHAMPIONSHIP

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.820
<i>He won the national title</i>
<i>in his senior year of high school.</i>

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:21.490
<i>After this victory, he quit wrestling.</i>

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.000
<i>He switched over to amateur boxing.</i>

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.160
<i>Despite his short career,</i>

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.590
<i>his natural talent led him to become</i>
<i>a member of the national team.</i>

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:34.130
INVITED TO NATIONAL TEAM
AFTER DEBUT

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:38.510
<i>However, not long after that,</i>
<i>he quit boxing.</i>

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:44.100
<i>Right after that, he knocked on</i>
<i>the door of mixed martial arts.</i>

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:46.180
<i>He was subjected to a cold stare</i>
<i>by the public.</i>

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:47.560
OHKUBO QUITS AGAIN

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.560
<i>People thought</i>
<i>he wouldn't last long at MMA, either.</i>

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.730
<i>But here is the fact people didn't know:</i>

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.030
<i>he didn't skip a single day</i>
<i>of wrestling practice,</i>

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.740
<i>even after he switched to boxing.</i>

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.530
<i>Ohkubo had noticed...</i>

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:07.870
<i>the importance of</i>
<i>grappling techniques in MMA.</i>

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.370
<i>It has been said...</i>

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:15.090
<i>that one's grappling skills are</i>
<i>100 percent proportional to their effort.</i>

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:20.340
<i>An amateur may be able to throw a punch</i>
<i>at a pro boxer by fluke,</i>

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.800
<i>but there are no flukes in grappling.</i>

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:25.640
<i>Everything happens...</i>

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.850
<i>for a reason.</i>

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.770
<i>A heel hold!</i>

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:44.410
<i>Agito dodged Ohkubo's stomp</i>
<i>and switched to an arm bar!</i>

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.240
<i>A neck throw to a scarf hold!</i>

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.240
<i>Oh, he's escaped again!</i>

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:51.540
<i>It's non-stop! They're going on and on!</i>

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.750
<i>Their battle keeps flowing without pause!</i>

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.710
<i>Ohkubo gets behind Agito!</i>

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.630
<i>Agito immediately locks him back!</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.930
<i>It's like two snakes</i>
<i>entangled with each other!</i>

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.680
<i>Neither of them is breaking down.</i>
<i>This is not a first-stage-level battle.</i>

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.810
COSMO IMAI

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.640
Atami,

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:16.110
that's quite a fighter
you've found yourself.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.230
Thank you, sir.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:24.320
I didn't choose to fight against the Fang
in the first round out of overconfidence.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:29.120
It was out of utter confidence
that Naoya Ohkubo could defeat him.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.540
<i>What's with him?</i>

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:42.470
<i>He showed he can grapple as good as me,</i>
<i>but let me mount him so easily?</i>

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:46.090
<i>And now he's not even trying to resist me.</i>

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:48.390
<i>Just barely guarding himself?</i>

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.890
<i>What the hell is he trying to do?</i>

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:53.390
That's enough.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:58.770
He sent Ohkubo flying
by the power of his hips alone?

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.450
What a child he is.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:10.200
It's like he just wanted to play
with Ohkubo as a warm-up,

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:14.750
even though I had instructed him
to go all-out from the start.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.670
<i>Barefaced lies.</i>

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:18.170
Anyway,

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.670
now it's time to see
Agito's true strength.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:25.170
The rehearsal is over.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:30.510
Now, I've seen all your
blows, throws, and grapples.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:35.690
You will never reach my level.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.360
It's over.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.320
Humans can't defeat monsters.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:48.700
Ohkubo's attacks won't be able to reach
the Fang anymore.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.080
RYO HIMURO

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.380
Temple...

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.560
<i>His opponent is unable to engage.</i>

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:22.900
<i>That's the forte of Naoya Ohkubo.</i>

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:27.900
<i>As its name suggests, mixed martial arts</i>
<i>combines various means of attack.</i>

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.410
BLOWS - THROWS
GRAPPLES - HOLDS

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:30.410
<i>This means...</i>

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.830
<i>its attacks are ever-changing.</i>

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.710
<i>Blows, throws, and grapples.</i>

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:42.290
<i>Agito's martial arts skills surpass</i>
<i>Ohkubo's in every area.</i>

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:47.550
<i>Does that mean there's no means</i>
<i>for Ohkubo to beat Agito?</i>

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.430
<i>No.</i>

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.470
<i>One skill individually would not be</i>
<i>enough, but all skills combined might be.</i>

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:56.600
<i>Ohkubo would respond to Agito's blows</i>
<i>with grapples.</i>

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:57.560
BLOW - GRAPPLE

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.770
<i>And he would fight back standing</i>
<i>to grappling.</i>

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:00.730
HOLD - THROW

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.230
BLOW TO THROW

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:05.650
<i>He would put Agito off his stride</i>
<i>and never allow him have his way.</i>

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.860
THROW TO HOLD

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:10.070
LEAVE

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.280
LEAVE TO GRAPPLE

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.700
GRAPPLE TO THROW

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.330
LEAVE TO THROW

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.790
<i>Whoa! Right in the face!</i>

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.330
<i>Is he dead? Is the Fang dead now?</i>

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:27.000
<i>Will the Fang finally be defeated?</i>

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:28.970
He's strong.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.590
Even Agito is having difficulty
dealing with him.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.390
That proves

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:38.720
that there is almost no break between
his blows, throws, locks, and holds.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:42.190
He doesn't need flashy techniques.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:45.150
The most powerful weapon he has

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:49.900
is his overwhelming proficiency
in the basic techniques.

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:51.400
What are you doing?

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.780
No time to hesitate, Ohkubo!
Don't forget, he's a monster!

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.290
No matter how many blows you throw,
you can't drop your guard!

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:00.500
<i>That's not it, Himuro.</i>

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.960
<i>I'm not dropping my guard.</i>

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.460
<i>That blow I dealt earlier...</i>

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.670
<i>I thought I had dealt a lethal kick.</i>

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.130
Just as I thought.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:17.050
I thought it was weird
that I didn't feel my kick hit you.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.520
That's not a human face.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.190
Hey, what's so funny?

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.360
I can see your face on the monitor.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.570
Okay, let's fight for one more round.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:39.540
<i>If he's able to stand after taking</i>
<i>my blow, he must've fended it off somehow.</i>

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.370
<i>He relaxed all muscles in his body</i>
<i>at the moment of attack</i>

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.130
<i>to disperse the shock.</i>

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:51.340
<i>That means he's dealing with my attacks.</i>

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:54.930
<i>That's freaking exciting!</i>

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:58.100
<i>You don't get to fight</i>
<i>someone like him often!</i>

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:01.930
<i>Block him from grappling!</i>

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:07.770
<i>He read my move?</i>

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.320
LEAVE TO

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:19.910
GRAPPLE

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.330
<i>Tilted vision.</i>

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:32.000
<i>That's where Ohkubo's memory ends.</i>

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.800
A belly-to-belly suplex!

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.560
Is that his revenge?

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:55.360
Naoya Ohkubo,

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.070
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.660
I have become even stronger...

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.410
thanks to you.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.540
Referee Yamamoto,

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.130
you should have stopped me much earlier.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.290
Bring him to a doctor.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.090
Bring me a stretcher now!

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:18.550
We have a winner!

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.850
The winner is Agito Kanoh!

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:25.980
<i>It... It's over!</i>

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.560
<i>The absolute champion</i>
<i>of mixed martial arts,</i>

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:34.360
the King of Combat, Naoya Ohkubo,
was knocked out with a single hit!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.820
That was a close one, wasn't it, Atami?

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.120
Agito's true value is in his evolution.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:49.000
It looks like he's reached
an even higher level through this match.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:54.670
I don't regret having Ohkubo
as our representative fighter.

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.260
One day, he will have another chance
to defeat the Fang.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:01.760
Ohkubo was fortunate.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:06.390
If he had matched Agito
a little more evenly,

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:10.980
he would definitely have lost his life.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.320
Ohkubo.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.950
I lost, didn't I?

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:24.870
What should I have done?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.000
I was good.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.250
I was keeping up with him
until halfway through.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:34.540
What the hell?

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.880
He evolved during the match.

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:43.300
How the hell was I supposed
to beat such a guy?

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:49.680
<i>There are surprisingly few fighters who</i>
<i>have died in fights with the fifth Fang.</i>

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:56.860
<i>However, most of those who fought him</i>
<i>were incapacitated as fighters.</i>

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.070
<i>The Fang kills one's fighting spirit.</i>

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:05.280
<i>He plants absolute terror in his opponent</i>
<i>and breaks their fangs...</i>

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:09.700
<i>just as his name "Fang" indicates.</i>

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:12.830
Kanoh.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.750
Wakatsuki. It's been a while.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:21.970
I watched your match with Gozo Murobuchi.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.760
You skills have improved again.

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.140
Oh.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.100
I haven't shown my everything yet.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:33.770
Will you be the one who wins
the left block of the tournament?

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:36.940
Man, really?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.320
You don't have a good eye
for fighters, do you?

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.610
The winner of the left block...

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.030
is going to be me.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:45.590
Hey, Ohma.

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.680
Kanoh has just finished his match.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:52.060
It's not a good idea to provoke him now.

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:55.140
No need for your concern.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:59.730
Your man wouldn't even be able
to leave a single scar on me.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.400
What the hell?

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:02.980
Ohma Tokita,

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.030
you are weak.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.740
There's no chance for you
to win the left block.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:12.080
Ohma!

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:16.660
Talk is cheap, you pomade-haired asshole.

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.960
Do you want me to prove to you

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:23.460
that I am stronger than you?

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:24.840
<i>You'd better not, Ohma.</i>

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:29.590
<i>As you are now,</i>
<i>you would only get yourself killed.</i>

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:32.850
NIKO TOKITA

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:33.810
Wha...

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:35.470
Niko?

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:37.140
<i>Is it surprising?</i>

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:40.600
<i>You didn't expect to see me</i>
<i>outside your mental world, did you?</i>

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.360
<i>You thought I was actually alive?</i>

00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:44.820
<i>Too bad.</i>

00:22:45.070 --> 00:22:48.030
<i>I'm just a figment you created.</i>

00:22:49.070 --> 00:22:51.740
<i>So, of course, those guys can't see me.</i>

00:22:52.530 --> 00:22:56.790
<i>Ohma, you are still... weak.</i>

00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.420
<i>You can't beat this guy...</i>

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:03.250
<i>nor this guy.</i>

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.750
<i>Not a chance.</i>

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:08.340
<i>Unless you use the Advance.</i>

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:15.850
<i>But if you did, all that's waiting</i>
<i>for you is inevitable death.</i>

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:20.390
<i>Your restraint is starting to</i>
<i>come off gradually.</i>

00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:26.480
<i>Whether or not you go forward,</i>
<i>you'll find yourself in a hell.</i>

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:31.450
I don't know
what the hell you're trying to say.

00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:36.120
I'm going to show you
that I'm stronger than anyone!

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:43.630
Ohma!

00:23:43.750 --> 00:23:45.590
It's out of the question.

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:51.130
Is it Raian that you'll fight
in the next match?

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:53.680
He is strong.

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:57.350
No matter how hard you try,
you don't stand a chance.

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.310
Let me tell you one more time.

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:04.650
You are weak.

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:06.940
PREVIEW

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:09.690
<i>The second stage of</i>
<i>Kengan Life-or-Death Tournament begins.</i>

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:13.950
<i>Attack, the King of Stranglers!</i>
<i>Control it, the Executioner!</i>

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:16.080
<i>Is this a mudslinging battle?</i>

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:18.410
<i>No, it's a deadly battle</i>
<i>beyond imagination.</i>

00:24:18.990 --> 00:24:20.330
<i>Next episode: "Abyss."</i>

00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:21.960
Subtitle translation by Miki Miyaji
